    "title": "Man arrested after incident on Haines Avenue - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gary Matthews ,\n11 hours ago RAPID CITY, S.D. – Rapid City police arrested a man following a late-night incident at the intersection of Haines Avenue and I-90.\nPolice say a man approached a vehicle at the intersection at around 11:20 p.m. and began yelling at the people inside the vehicle.\nThe man brandished a knife and at one point, stuck it through the open window of the victim’s vehicle.\nThe man then fled the scene in his vehicle.\nPolice noticed the suspect vehicle in the drive-through of a restaurant on Haines Avenue and initiated a felony-level traffic stop. The driver, identified as 35-year-old Quitan Chee of Rapid City, was detained and placed under arrest for Aggravated Assault Intimidation and Driving without a Valid License.\nNo injuries were reported.\n2",
    "summary": "– Rapid City police arrested a man following a late-night incident at the intersection of Haines Avenue and I-90. Police say a man approached a vehicle at the intersection at around 11:20 p.m. and began yelling at the people inside the vehicle. The man brandished a knife and at one point, stuck it through the open window of the victim’s vehicle. Police noticed the suspect vehicle in the drive-through of a restaurant on Haines Avenue and initiated a felony-level traffic stop.",
